    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0162" n="82" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg82"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/787c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chairman of the
                        American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-25T21:00:00-05:00">March 25, 1930—9
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>260. Our telegrams Nos. 258 and 259, March 25, 7 p.m. and 8 p.m., respectively,
                    were written after we had read your No. 161, <pb facs="0163" n="83"
                        xml:id="pg83"/> March 25, 5 p.m. The matter is assuming considerable
                    seriousness over here, and the President is bothered. I am amazed at the cable
                    advices of which Stone is the source.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
